# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Dustfile — Cleanup and hygiene contract for progblocks
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell (hyperpolymath)
#
# What should be cleaned up (exnovated) or clearly re-labelled. Housekeeping,
# not blockers — see ../bust/Bustfile.a2ml for what's actually broken.

@abstract:
Cleanup and hygiene items for progblocks. view-manager.js, the largest
dead-code item, was deleted on 2026-10-05 (with exporter.js and
smart-paste.js). What remains are the unimported stubs a2ml-parser.js and
k9-validator.js and the tree-sitter-a2ml.wasm placeholder (not real
WebAssembly). None is a runtime bug on its own — all are exnovation
candidates that mislead a reader of the source tree into thinking more is
wired up than actually is.
@end

## Dead Code

### view-manager-unreferenced (RESOLVED 2026-10-05 — deleted)
- description: src/modules/view-manager.js (55 lines) was never imported by anything, yet held the only real linter/WebSocket code while the component rendered a hardcoded '<i>Linter ready</i>' string. Both were deleted on 2026-10-05; a linter is out of charter
- run: test ! -e src/modules/view-manager.js
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: this probe
- notes: The delete path was taken. If a linter is ever wanted, it returns as a real change with tests, not as an unimported module.

### a2ml-parser-stub
- description: src/a2ml-parser.js (60 lines) has its tree-sitter path commented out; the A2MLState class is dead code; nothing imports the module (the component uses its own tokenize())
- run: grep -q 'tree-sitter' src/a2ml-parser.js
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

### wasm-placeholder
- description: assets/tree-sitter-a2ml.wasm is a 118-byte ASCII text placeholder ("// Dummy WASM file placeholder"), not real WebAssembly
- run: test "$(stat -c%s assets/tree-sitter-a2ml.wasm 2>/dev/null || stat -f%z assets/tree-sitter-a2ml.wasm)" -lt 1000
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)
- notes: Either vendor a real compiled artefact or remove the file — a fake .wasm sitting in assets/ implies a working parser that does not exist.

### fake-validator-methods
- description: k9-validator.js's validateNickel() fakes a 50ms setTimeout then unconditionally returns {valid:true, errors:[]}; executeJustTask() console.logs and returns true. Neither is called by anything, and since 2026-10-05 nothing imports the module.
- run: grep -q 'setTimeout' src/k9-validator.js
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)

## Version Drift

### version-string-disagreement (RESOLVED 2026-10-05 — all fields aligned on 0.3.0)
- description: package.k9 and contracts.ncl said 1.0.0; progblocks.launcher.a2ml and progblocks-launcher.sh said 0.1.0; package.json said 0.3.0. The run line now detects a regression: it matches only if a field has drifted off 0.3.0 again
- run: ! grep -qE '"(1\.0\.0|0\.1\.0)"' contracts.ncl package.k9 progblocks.launcher.a2ml progblocks-launcher.sh
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: not yet automated (documentary)
- notes: Resolve to one version before any tag is cut — see ../descriptiles/PLAYBOOK.a2ml release-process.

## Build Recipe Honesty

### fake-build-recipe (RESOLVED — recipe removed)
- description: Justfile's build recipe used to cat-concatenate ES modules into one file without stripping import/export syntax, producing a file that could not run as a script. Rather than fix it, the recipe was deleted; there is no `build:` recipe in the Justfile at all now.
- run: "! grep -q '^build:' Justfile"
- severity: info
- enforced-by: this probe
- notes: If a real bundle step is ever needed, use a real bundler (esbuild) — do not re-add a recipe that only implies one exists.
